    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are headlined today by **Gunnar Henderson**, who registers a dominant 83.29 efficiency score against Hancock. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive park factor boost (+16%) and a favorable platoon advantage, making him our primary engine for counting stats. **Jackson Merrill** (60.85) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (60.35) also clear the \"Strong\" threshold; **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is particularly well-positioned due to favorable wind conditions (+5%) and a strong #2 spot in the order, while **Jackson Merrill** enjoys a rare positive SP skill matchup against Abbott. Conversely, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (58.89) is forced to contend with S\u00e1nchez\u2019s elite 2.74 xERA, which suppresses his ceiling despite his high-leverage spot in the lineup.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Brayan Rocchio**, who narrowly missed the starting cut with a 40.07 score. While **Brayan Rocchio** offers utility, the combination of a middling SP matchup against Warren and a detrimental #9 spot in the batting order rendered his daily efficiency inferior to the rest of the utility block. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** (42.89) and **Curtis Mead** (48.37) remain in the lineup despite being in the marginal category; their inclusion is necessitated by the absence of **Kyle Tucker**, who is idle today, and the continued IL status of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. Managers should note that **Nasim Nunez** faces an elite defensive catcher, which, combined with the #9 order slot, caps his overall upside despite his speed profile. We continue to monitor the status of our depth pieces like **Andy Pages**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Heliot Ramos** to ensure we aren't leaving stolen base potential on the bench should late-breaking lineup changes occur.",
